    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "text-left",
      "content": {
        "title": "Know who owns every number",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Owners, descriptions and certification status are part of each model’s definition. The catalog shows them next to lineage and health, so anyone deciding whether to rely on a table can see who maintains it, how fresh it is and whether its tests passed on the latest run."
        ],
        "primary": {
          "label": "Explore catalog",
          "href": "/product/catalog"
        },
        "tertiary": {
          "label": "Read guide",
          "href": "/learn"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "illustration.diagram",
          "alt": "The discovery loop: search, inspect, trace, trust, reuse, document",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/split/catalog.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "columns": "7/5",
        "topPadding": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "media-left",
      "content": {
        "title": "Contracts for shared data",
        "paragraphs": [
          "A contract declares the columns, types and guarantees a model promises to the teams that depend on it. Breaking changes are caught in review, and versioned models give downstream teams time to migrate on their own schedule instead of discovering a problem in production."
        ],
        "primary": {
          "label": "Learn more",
          "href": "/product/mesh"
        },
        "tertiary": {
          "label": "Read the documentation on contracts",
          "href": "/learn"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
          "alt": "Five team projects connected around a shared finance project",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/hero/mesh.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "columns": "5/7",
        "topPadding": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "text-left",
      "content": {
        "title": "Audit everything, easily",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Every deployment, permission change and sign-in is recorded with who did it and when. Export the log for your security tools, or search it directly when an auditor asks how a figure in last quarter’s report was produced and who approved the change."
        ],
        "primary": {
          "label": "Talk to us about compliance today",
          "href": "/contact"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "illustration.diagram",
          "alt": "The release loop: merge, build, check, promote, schedule, notify",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/split/deploy.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "columns": "7/5",
        "topPadding": "default"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "content.media-split",
      "variant": "media-left",
      "content": {
        "title": "Policies for people and agents",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Assistants and automated agents follow the same access rules as the people who use them. They can only read the projects and environments their user can reach, and every request they make is logged, so adopting AI does not mean opening a new back door to your data."
        ],
        "primary": {
          "label": "See how agents are governed",
          "href": "/product/analyst"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
          "alt": "Catalog search results with owners and certification",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/tabs/dark-8.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
